# Vespa — health, deployment state, metrics
# VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" above each block.
# See ./README.md for setup. Fields/ports come from
# src/learnarken/vespa/app/schemas/chunk.sd and docs/local-services.md.

@config = http://localhost:19071
@query  = http://localhost:8080

### Config server up? (the Day 3 readiness signal — answers before any deploy)
GET {{config}}/state/v1/health

### Query container up? (only answers AFTER an application package is deployed)
GET {{query}}/state/v1/health

### Which application generation is live (deploy took effect?)
GET {{config}}/application/v2/tenant/default/application/default

### Full deployed services config — confirms the chunk schema is in the package
GET {{config}}/application/v2/tenant/default/application/default/environment/prod/region/default/instance/default/content/

# Cluster-controller state ("up" per node, buckets out of sync) lives on port
# 19050, which this container does not publish to the host — REST Client cannot
# reach it. Use the container's own curl:
#   docker exec learnarken-vespa curl -s localhost:19050/cluster/v2/learnarken

### Container metrics (query latency, feed rate, memory)
GET {{query}}/state/v1/metrics

### Search-node metrics: doc count, attribute + index memory (embedding is 4096 floats/doc)
GET {{query}}/metrics/v2/values

### Application-level status — build info, container components
GET {{query}}/ApplicationStatus
